From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:34:03 +0200
Subject: settings: viewing range 60 by default on the PS3, not 190

Luanti's default viewing range of 190 nodes is far beyond what 217 MB of
RAM and the PPE can generate, mesh and draw: the benchmark flight over a
fresh world (gamedb:luanti's recipe, variant view190) ran at 15 fps steady
with 56 s of frames over 100 ms in its 135 s window and a 1% low of 3 fps,
against 46 fps, 2.3 s and 18 fps at 60, in the same boot (2026-10-28,
Mesa ps3.924, kernel .874). The played session of 2026-10-24, on the
default, had 25 s of stutter a minute. 60 is what every benchmark of the
game has measured; the fog comes nearer. The Settings menu and a
minetest.conf that names viewing_range still change it.

Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/src/defaultsettings.cpp b/src/defaultsettings.cpp
--- a/src/defaultsettings.cpp
+++ b/src/defaultsettings.cpp
@@ -245,7 +245,9 @@ void set_default_settings()
 	settings->setDefault("tooltip_append_itemname", "false");
 	settings->setDefault("fps_max", "60");
 	settings->setDefault("fps_max_unfocused", "10");
-	settings->setDefault("viewing_range", "190");
+	// Walnut (PS3): 60, not 190: at 190 the fresh world flight ran at 15 fps with 56 s of stalls in
+	// 135 s, at 60 at 46 fps with 2.3 s (same boot, 2026-10-28); 256 MB of RAM and the PPE set it
+	settings->setDefault("viewing_range", "60");
 	settings->setDefault("client_mesh_chunk", "1");
 	settings->setDefault("screen_w", "1024");
 	settings->setDefault("screen_h", "600");
